From: Rishi Malhotra <rishi_malhotra@redwood.ai>
To: Camila Reyes <camila_reyes@redwood.ai>, Marissa Cole <marissa@redwood.ai>, Sam Taylor <sam.taylor@finlytics.com>
Date: 2026-06-19T08:45:00-07:00
Subject: Re: Follow-up: Integration discovery + 5xx repro (embeddings -> reranker)

Hi all — I pulled the logs for the time window around 2026-06-18T15:58:12Z. Quick findings:

- The 500s are coming from our inference gateway (504/500/502 clusters intermittently), not the model process itself. Root cause looks like transient memory pressure combined with large request bodies hitting the gateway worker pool.
- We also saw a small percentage of malformed JSON from a different test client causing a parsing error; that would return 400, not 500 — so separate but noted.

Immediate recommendations (quick to apply):
1) Client changes (Sam):
   - Increase timeout to 30s.
   - Add 3 retries with exponential backoff on 5xx (Jitter recommended).
   - Reduce rerank candidate count to top-25 for initial POC throughput testing.

2) Payload optimizations:
   - Strip non-essential metadata from each candidate before sending (e.g., only include title + snippet + doc_id and vector index).
   - Use compressed payloads if your client supports Content-Encoding: gzip. Example curl:

   curl -X POST https://api.redwood.ai/v1/rerank \
     -H "Authorization: Bearer <API_KEY>" \
     -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
     --data-binary @sample-payload.json.gz \
     --compressed

3) Server-side mitigation (our side):
   - We'll add a temporary increase to gateway worker pool for your account for the POC window.
   - We'll also search for any recent deploys that coincided with the time window.

SDK snippet (Node) recommendation for retries & timeout:

   // pseudocode - adapt to your SDK
   const client = new RedwoodClient({ apiKey: process.env.REDWOOD_KEY, timeout: 30000 });
   async function rerankWithRetry(payload) {
     let attempt = 0;
     while (attempt < 4) {
       try {
         return await client.rerank(payload);
       } catch (err) {
         if (!is5xx(err) || attempt === 3) throw err;
         await sleep(2 ** attempt * 100 + jitter());
         attempt++;
       }
     }
   }

Sam — can you try the client-side changes and confirm whether the 5xx frequency drops? We'll monitor the gateway logs and report back by 6/19 EOD.

Thanks,
Rishi
Senior Support Engineer | Redwood Inference
